{title: 649 - Lord, While for All Mankind We Pray}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #649 • DUNFERMLINE • 16.14}
{lyricist: John R. Wreford}
{composer: Scottish Psalter}
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 649}
{meta: tune DUNFERMLINE}
{meta: meter 16.14}
{meta: category Christian Life - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Dm/A]Lord, while [Gm]for [F]all [Bb/F]mankind [C]we [F/C]pray, Of [Bb]every [G]clime [C/G]and coast,
[F/C]Oh, [C]hear [Bb]us [Am]for [Bb]our native [C]land, [F/C]The [C7/Bb]land [F]we [G7]love [C/G]the [Dm/A]most!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Dm/A]O guard [F]our [Bb/F]shores [F/C]from [Bb]every [C/G]foe,
[Dm/A]With [Gm]peace [C/G]our [F/C]borders [G]bless;
[F/C]With [C]prosperous [Bb]times [F/C]our [C7/Bb]cities [C/G]crown,
[F/C]Our [Bb]fields with [C]plenteousness!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Dm/A]Unite [Bb/F]us [C]in [F/C]the [C/G]sacred [G]love
[Dm/A]Of [Gm]knowledge, [F/C]truth, [C/G]and [G]Thee;
[F/C]And [C]let [Am]our [Bb]hills [C]and [F/C]valleys [C/G]shout
[F/C]The [Bb]songs of [C]liberty.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[Dm/A]Lord of [F]the [C/G]nations, [Bb]thus [C/G]to Thee
[Dm/A]Our [Gm]country [F/C]we [C/G]commend;
[F/C]Be [C]Thou [Am]her [Bb]Refuge [F/C]and her [C/G]trust,
[F/C]Her [Bb]everlasting [G7]friend.
{end_of_verse}
